hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18111","Abu Usamah, Hammad ibn Usamah, narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, narrated to us, from his father who said: A neighbor of Khadijah bint Khuwaylid narrated to me that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying to Khadijah: O Khadijah, by Allah I will never worship al-Lat and al-Uzza; by Allah I will never worship. He said: So Khadijah says: Leave al-Lat, leave al-Uzza. He said: They were their idols which they used to worship, then they would lie down."
